# Strapi Cloud image upload (production)

## Production policy (mandatory)

- **Production Cloud images must be durable on S3.** Do **not** use ephemeral Cloud `/uploads/` (migration base64 / `finish:collection-images-on-cloud`) as the production path.
- Strapi Cloud **disk is ephemeral**. A Strapi **release/redeploy** deletes files under `/uploads/` even when DB `image` / `cover` relations still point at them → live site shows placeholders; `HEAD` returns **404**.
- **After any Strapi Cloud deploy**, verify production media URLs are `https://…amazonaws.com/…` (or the configured S3 host). If they are `/uploads/…`, re-run the **S3** push — not the ephemeral finish script.
- Frontend (`mosc-temp`) resolves relative URLs via `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRAPI_URL` + `getMediaUrl` — fix Cloud/S3 files, not the Next app.

```bash
# ✅ DO — durable production default
npm run push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2 --skip-api

# ❌ DON'T — ephemeral (wiped on next Cloud deploy)
npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

**Verified (Jul 2026):** Institutions for `mosc_malankara_orthodox_2` looked fine after ephemeral finish, then broke after a Strapi release deploy. S3 register fixed **219/219** with `HEAD 200` on `eventapp-media-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com`.

## When images are missing on production

- Content/tenant links exist on Cloud, but cards show placeholders or broken images.
- API `populate=image` (or `cover`) returns a URL, but `HEAD` is **404**.
- Symptom of ephemeral path: `image.url` like `/uploads/ca_….jpeg` (relative) instead of S3.
- Local `http://localhost:3000/...` can still look fine — local `public/uploads/` is unaffected by Cloud redeploy.

## Production vs demo tenant (critical)

| Audience | Tenant ID |
|---|---|
| Live site (`www.mosc-temp.com`, Amplify) | **`mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`** |
| Editor / demo CMS | `tenant_demo_002` |

Always pass `--tenant-id=` explicitly. In [scripts/lib/liturgy-cli.js](mdc:scripts/lib/liturgy-cli.js), **CLI flags override `.env` `TENANT_ID`** — confirm the log line `Tenant: mosc_malankara_orthodox_2` before trusting the run.

## News push gotchas (articles + ads)

- **`push:tenant-to-cloud` publish resets `publishedAt` to “now”.** After pushing articles, restore historical dates from local:
  ```bash
  node scripts/sync-article-published-dates-to-cloud.js --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
  ```
  Uses `POST /api/migration/fix-published` (knex) so Document Service publish does not overwrite dates again.
- **S3 register with `prod/` prefix while local media lives under `dev/`** creates Cloud URLs that **403** (object missing under prod). `push-collection-images-s3` now copies remote `dev/` bytes into the prod key before register. Emergency repair:
  ```bash
  node scripts/repair-cloud-ad-s3-from-dev.js
  ```
- Bucket has **ACLs disabled** — do not pass `ACL: public-read` on PutObject; rely on bucket policy for the prefix.

## Two upload strategies

### A — Durable (S3 + register-s3-media) — **default for production**

Use for any production / live-tenant image fix. Survives Strapi Cloud redeploys.

```bash
# Stop local Strapi first (script embeds Strapi to read local DB).
# Requires .env: STRAPI_CLOUD_URL, STRAPI_CLOUD_API_TOKEN, AWS_* (see below)
npm run push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2 --skip-api
# optional flags: --skip-s3 | --link-existing | omit --skip-api to try Cloud /api/upload first
npm run push:all-collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

- Needs local `.env` AWS creds (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_S3_BUCKET_NAME`) writing to shared prod prefix (`S3_UPLOAD_PREFIX`, default `strapi-editorial-media/prod`).
- Prefer Node matching local `better-sqlite3` (often Node 22 on this machine) if default shell Node breaks native modules.
- ACL: omit when bucket is “Bucket owner enforced” — [strapi-s3-upload-acl-fix.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strapi-s3-upload-acl-fix.mdc).
- Details: [STRAPI_MEDIA_STORAGE_S3_CLOUD_PRD.html](mdc:documentation/STRAPI_MEDIA_STORAGE_S3_CLOUD_PRD.html).

**Success criteria:** every `image.url` (or `cover` / `cardImage` / `pdf`) is an **S3 absolute URL** and `HEAD` returns **200**.

### B — Ephemeral quick fix (migration base64 → Cloud local disk) — **emergency only**

Use **only** when S3/AWS is unavailable and you need a temporary unblock. Expect images to **break again on the next Cloud deploy**.

```bash
npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
# Batch (still ephemeral):
npm run finish:all-collection-images-on-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

- Success log looks like: `Created: 9 | Linked: 219`
- Windows may exit non-zero with `UV_HANDLE_CLOSING` after success — treat **Created/Linked** as the result.
- **Must** follow up with strategy A (S3) before considering production done.
- Agent must **warn** the user that this will not survive redeploy.

