## Workflow (institutions — production)

1. Confirm local has files under `public/uploads/` and Cloud entries exist for **`mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`**.
2. Stop local Strapi (`npm run develop`).
3. Run **durable S3**:
   ```bash
   npm run push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2 --skip-api
   ```
4. Verify Cloud API: `GET /api/institutions?filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2&populate[0]=image` — every `image.url` must be **S3** and `HEAD` **200** (not `/uploads/...`).
5. Spot-check: [https://www.mosc-temp.com/mosc-redesign/institutions-cms](https://www.mosc-temp.com/mosc-redesign/institutions-cms).
6. After a later Strapi Cloud release deploy: spot-check again. If URLs regress to `/uploads/`, re-run step 3 (S3). Do **not** “fix” with ephemeral finish alone.

## Agent invocation

- User: *“Upload / fix Cloud images for Institutions on production”* or *“images missing after Strapi deploy”*
- Agent: run **`push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud`** (or batch S3) with **`mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`** unless user names another tenant; do not ask the user to run it.
- Do **not** default to `finish:collection-images-on-cloud` for production.
- Read master doc: [cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html](mdc:documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html) + per-type PRD under `documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/`.

## Adding a new collection

1. Register in [cloud-image-migration-config.js](mdc:scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js) (`uid`, `table`, `tenantLinkTable`, `entryIdCol`, `restPlural`, `mediaField`).
2. Document § Cloud image upload fix in the type’s `*-production-cloud-push-prd.html` — production path = **S3**, ephemeral = emergency only.
3. Deploy Cloud if migration/`register-s3-media` endpoints changed, then run **S3** push for the production tenant (and demo if needed).
